{"type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "video", "id": 2, "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"video_src": "engenn8le15ob03re2vid02", "images": [{"image": "", "text": "", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"image": "", "text": "<p>How many of the foods you eat are genetically modified? What potential dangers might we be faced with by eating GMOs?</p>\n<p>I am not certain that anyone knows what the long-term effects of eating genetically modified foods could be. One scientist who studies how lab rats are affected by eating GMO potatoes has stated, \"In my personal view, increasing research shows that GMOs may actually be very unsafe.\"</p>", "time": "5", "id": 1}, {"image": "", "text": "In my opinion, unpredicted allergic reactions could be caused by using proteins from organisms that are not part of the human food chain. For example, corn only suitable for animal feed is found in taco shells. As I see it, we could be harmed by this corn, because it's been genetically modified to contain a toxin that isn't broken down in human gastric systems.", "time": "24500", "id": 2}, {"image": "", "text": "<p>Furthermore, I think that disease-carrying bacteria could be made resistant to antibiotics by genetic modification. Antibiotic-resistant genes are used as 'markers' in GMO crops. These marker genes can be digested by the stomach. The result? We could be infected with antibiotic-resistant bacteria.</p>\n<p>So, the next time you buy food, look at the label for GMOs. Consider the statement issued by the British Medical Association saying that antibiotic resistance developing in microorganisms is one major health threat that we will face in the 21st century.</p>", "time": "48500", "id": 3}]}}], "_data": []}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about technology and subjects of stud