content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: <span class=\"bullet\">Listen to the audio.</span> <span class=\"bullet\">Type in the missing words. </span><span class=\"bullet\">Use capital letters where necessary.</span>  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You have 2 attempts to submit your answers.", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Science, Old and New", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Is Genetic Engineering Safe?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 15, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Passive Voice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use an active structure when you want the  \"doer\" of the action to be the subject.<br/> You use a passive structure when you want the \"receiver\" of the action to be the subject. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Active sentence = <span class=\"italic\">When you</span> (subject)<span class=\"italic\"> mix the powder </span>(object)<span class=\"italic\"> with water, it becomes a potion.</span><br/>Passive sentence = <span class=\"italic\">When the powder </span>(subject)<span class=\"italic\"> is mixed with water, it becomes a potion. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It is not necessary to mention the subject from an active sentence when it is changed to a passive sentence. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You make the passive form of a verb by using tenses of the be verb followed by the past participle. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Simple Present passive form is:<br/><br/> am/are/is + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Antibiotic-resistant genes <span class=\"strong\">are used</span> as \"markers\" in GMO crops.  </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "How many of the foods you eat are genetically modified?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "For example, corn only suitable for animal feed is found in taco shells.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They contain a toxin that isn't broken down in human gastric systems.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "One scientist studies how lab rats are affected after eating GMO potatoes.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Modal Verbs in the Passive Voice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use modal verbs to add meaning to other verbs. They come before the dictionary form (Infinitive without <span class=\"italic\">to</span>) of the main verb. <br/> Modal verbs can add meaning connected with certainty or obligation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " You can use modal verbs in the passive voice. <br/> You use the passive voice when you want to focus on the receiver  of the action, rather than the \"doer\" of the action. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Here is the structure of a passive sentence:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + To be + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">We  <span class=\"strong\">are infected</span> with an antibiotic-resistant bacteria.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can add a modal verb before the To be.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + modal + To be + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": " For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">We <span class=\"strong\">could be</span> infected with an  antibiotic-resistant bacteria.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Here the sentence now has an additional  meaning of possibility, thanks to the modal <span class=\"strong\">could</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What potential dangers might we be faced with by eating GMOs? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I am not certain that anyone knows what the long-term effects of eating genetically modified foods could be.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "GMOs may actually be very unsafe. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Unpredicted allergic reactions could be caused by using proteins from organisms that are not part of the human food chain. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We could be harmed by this corn, because it's been genetically modified.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I think that disease-carrying bacteria could be made resistant to antibiotics by genetic modification. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "These marker genes can be digested by the stomach.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "modified", "type": "name"}, {"content": " changed in form or character", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: How many of the foods you eat are genetically modified?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about GMOs.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "resistance", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the ability of an object to not be affected by external factors", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Antibiotic resistance developing in microorganisms is one major health threat that we will face in the 21st century.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "long-term", "type": "name"}, {"content": "continuing to exist or to have an effect for a long time in the future", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I am not certain that anyone knows what the long-term effects of eating genetically modified foods could be.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "unsafe", "type": "name"}, {"content": "dangerous", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Increasing research shows that GMOs may actually be very unsafe.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "allergic", "type": "name"}, {"content": "affected by an allergy", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Allergic reactions are caused by multiple external factors in the environment. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "unpredicted", "type": "name"}, {"content": "without warning or announcement", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Unpredicted allergic reactions could be caused by proteins from organisms that are not part of the human food chain.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "organism", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a living thing that has the ability to act or function independently", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Organisms that are not part of the human food chain could cause allergic reactions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "toxin", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a poisonous substance that causes disease", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Usually, genetically modified food contains a great amount of toxins.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob03aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to break down", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to dissolve", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Corn has been genetically modified to contain a toxin that isn't broken down in human gastric systems.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le15ob03aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Read up on GMOs, what they are and how they may affect us.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write 5 to 8 questions to ask other people about GMOs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask 4 people all of your questions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the answers and write two or three paragraphs explaining what people do and do not know about GMOs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your findings with a partner or the class.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about technology and gene modification. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask about possibility, necessity, and certainty of what may happen with GMO food. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain my opinion.", "type": "text"}]}]}